# Data conversion between byte and gibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and gibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0000GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0000GiB; backward, converting 1GiB to 1073741824B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GiB yields 1610612736.0B. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(GiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(GiB))
backward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0000GiB
0.0000GiB
1073741824B
1610612736.0B

<<< stderr
